<div class="docs-world-page">

    <div class="docs-eyebrow">ENGINE / WORLD DATA</div>

    <h1>
        World &amp; <span class="docs-accent">chunk storage</span>
    </h1>

    <p class="docs-lead">
        The current world implementation stores chunks by horizontal
        chunk coordinate and represents block and light data in flat arrays.
    </p>

    <h2>Chunk dimensions</h2>

    <div class="docs-stat-grid">
        <div>
            <strong>32</strong>
            <span>Blocks along X</span>
        </div>

        <div>
            <strong>32</strong>
            <span>Blocks along Z</span>
        </div>

        <div>
            <strong>416</strong>
            <span>Blocks along Y</span>
        </div>

        <div>
            <strong>16</strong>
            <span>Blocks per mesh section height</span>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p>
        A concrete <code>Crafty.ChunkGeneration.World.Chunk</code> has
        <code>Size = 32</code>, <code>Height = 416</code>, and
        <code>Volume = Size × Size × Height</code>.
    </p>

    <p>
        The mesh pipeline uses 26 vertical sections, each split into a
        2 × 2 grid horizontally (four 16 × 16 × 16 sections per vertical layer).
    </p>

    <h2>Block representation</h2>

    <p>
        The SDK defines <code>BlockPlacement</code> as a readonly value
        containing a <code>uint Id</code> and a <code>byte State</code>.
        A chunk stores a flat <code>BlockPlacement[]</code>.
        The current index calculation is:
    </p>

    <div class="docs-code-card">
        <div class="docs-code-title">
            <span>CHUNK INDEX</span>
            <span>FROM Chunk.GetIndex</span>
        </div>

        <pre><code>index = x * (Size * Height) + z * Height + y;</code></pre>
    </div>

    <p>
        In other words, Y is the contiguous inner dimension, Z is the
        next dimension, and X is the outer dimension. Coordinates passed
        to the chunk's local block methods are chunk-local; the
        <code>World</code> class maps world X/Z coordinates to chunk
        coordinates and local coordinates.
    </p>

    <h2>World access and block changes</h2>

    <p>
        <code>World</code> stores loaded chunks in a
        <code>ConcurrentDictionary&lt;(int X, int Z), IChunk&gt;</code>.
        <code>GetBlock</code> returns the default placement if the
        requested chunk is not loaded.
    </p>

    <p>
        <code>SetBlock</code> returns without changing anything if the
        chunk is not loaded; otherwise it writes the placement, marks
        the chunk modified, and raises <code>BlockChanged</code> with
        old and new block IDs.
    </p>

    <p>
        <code>MainWindow</code> subscribes to <code>BlockChanged</code>.
        The handler updates sky lighting and marks the corresponding
        world mesh block dirty so a later update job can rebuild
        affected geometry.
    </p>

    <h2>Lighting storage</h2>

    <p>
        Each chunk has one byte of light data per block. The upper
        four bits hold sky light and the lower four bits hold block
        light.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-code-card">
        <div class="docs-code-title">
            <span>LIGHT BYTE LAYOUT</span>
            <span>4 BITS + 4 BITS</span>
        </div>

        <div class="docs-light-layout">
            <div class="docs-light-part docs-light-sky">
                <strong>SKY LIGHT</strong>
                <span>Upper 4 bits</span>
            </div>

            <div class="docs-light-part docs-light-block">
                <strong>BLOCK LIGHT</strong>
                <span>Lower 4 bits</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <p>
        <code>GetSkyLight</code>, <code>GetBlockLight</code>, and
        <code>SetLight</code> expose the nibble representation;
        values are clamped to 0–15.
    </p>

    <h2>Persistence</h2>

    <p>
        A world is stored as a directory containing a
        <code>&lt;name&gt;.world</code> file and a <code>chunks</code>
        directory.
    </p>

    <p>
        The world file is Deflate-compressed and contains the name and
        64-bit seed. Chunk files are also Deflate-compressed and store
        block count, modification state, and each block's uint ID plus
        byte state.
    </p>

    <p>
        Missing chunks are generated on demand and saved. On quit,
        modified chunks are saved and unchanged chunk files are deleted
        by the current save workflow.
    </p>

    <div class="docs-callout docs-callout-warning">
        <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>

        <div>
            <strong>Do not hard-code storage assumptions into mods</strong>

            <p>
                The flat-array layout and file format are implementation
                details of this repository snapshot. Use SDK interfaces
                where available; direct access to the concrete chunk
                implementation couples code to the current storage format.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

